#!/usr/bin/env python3
# apply_lvb_sl_spot.py — fence LVB_SL_SPOT_20261029
#   requires LVB_V1_20261023 + LVB_V1_FIX1_20261023 (already on main)
# ============================================================================
# Levels page ("Tripwire" / LVB_V1), 2026-10-29:
#
# 1. CANCEL (and three more buttons) DID NOTHING in the desktop app.
#    The page used window.confirm(); Tauri's webview silently returns false,
#    so Cancel, Square off, Square off all and the Live / Paper+Live mode
#    switch returned before sending anything (reproduced: 3 Cancel clicks →
#    0 requests). Fix: no confirm() at all — every one of those is TWO-TAP
#    like the other panels (first tap arms 4 s and relabels "Tap again …",
#    second tap acts). Off / Paper stay one tap.
#
# 2. SL is SPOT POINTS measured FROM THE LIMIT (was % of option premium),
#    the same convention as TP:  CE stop = spot ≤ Upper − SL,
#    PE stop = spot ≥ Lower + SL. Defaults NIFTY 25 / SENSEX 75, editable,
#    required (> 0). SL is checked before TP each 2 s poll; exits still fill
#    at the option LTP. The page shows each side's SL and TP levels.
#
#    Existing data: lvb_conditions gains sl_pts + sl_spot in place (ALTER
#    TABLE ADD COLUMN, automatic on the first read — no migration step).
#    A row created BEFORE this change keeps its old premium-% stop, so a
#    trade opened under it is managed as it was sold; editing such an ARMED
#    row converts it to spot points. paper_trades.sl_price is now 0 for LVB
#    rows (the stop is a spot level, never a premium).
#
# FILES (whole-file swap, LVB-owned only; each must be byte-identical to the
# delivered version or the script aborts):
#   backend/app/engine/lvb/{lvb_core,lvb_repo,lvb_manager,test_lvb}.py
#   backend/app/api/lvb_routes.py      frontend/src/pages/LevelBreak.jsx
#   (+ desktop/src-tauri/backend/app/… if present)
# Run from the repo root:  python3 apply_lvb_sl_spot.py   then build-scalp.sh
# Verified before delivery: LVB suite 65/65 (incl. legacy-row + old-table
# migration), routes via ASGI, Chromium UI 34/34 with confirm() returning
# false, react-scripts build "Compiled successfully" (0 warnings).
# ============================================================================
